169 |   "content": "{\n  \"filePath\": \"CLAUDE.md\",\n  \"content\": \"1 | # CLAUDE.md\\r\\n2 | \\r\\n3 | This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\\r\\n4 | \\r\\n5 | ## Development Commands\\r\\n6 | \\r\\n7 | | Command | Description |\\r\\n8 | |---------|-------------|\\r\\n9 | | `pnpm typecheck` | Type check without emitting files |\\r\\n10 | | `pnpm build` | Build for production (outputs to `dist/`) |\\r\\n11 | | `pnpm dev` | Run CLI interactive mode |\\r\\n12 | | `pnpm dev:demo` | Run demo mode (non-interactive) |\\r\\n13 | | `pnpm dev:cli [sessionId]` | Run CLI with optional session ID |\\r\\n14 | \\r\\n15 | ## Environment Configuration\\r\\n16 | \\r\\n17 | The app uses environment-specific `.env` files loaded by dotenv:\\r\\n18 | - `.env.development` - Development environment\\r\\n19 | - `.env.production` - Production environment\\r\\n20 | \\r\\n21 | Required environment variables:\\r\\n22 | - `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` - API key for LLM provider\\r\\n23 | - `DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL` - Base URL for LLM API\\r\\n24 | \\r\\n25 | ## Architecture Overview\\r\\n26 | \\r\\n27 | This is a multi-session AI agent built with **Domain-Driven Design (DDD)** and **Repository Pattern**.\\r\\n28 | \\r\\n29 | ```\\r\\n30 | ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\r\\n31 | │                         CLI Layer                           │\\r\\n32 | │  (src/cli/) - Interactive commands, readline with history   │\\r\\n33 | └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\\r\\n34 |                               │\\r\\n35 | ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\r\\n36 | │                         Agent                               │\\r\\n37 | │  (src/agent/) - Orchestrates LLM calls and sessions         │\\r\\n38 | └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\\r\\n39 |                               │\\r\\n40 |          ┌────────────────────┼────────────────────┐\\r\\n41 |          │                    │                    │\\r\\n42 | ┌────────▼─────────┐  ┌───────▼────────┐  ┌───────▼─────────┐\\r\\n43 | │   Domain Layer   │  │ Application   │  │ Infrastructure  │\\r\\n44 | │ (src/domain/)    │  │ (src/app/)    │  │ (src/infra/)    │\\r\\n45 | │ - Session        │  │ SessionMgr    │  │ MessageRepo     │\\r\\n46 | │ - MessageQueue   │  │               │  │                 │\\r\\n47 | └──────────────────┘  └───────────────┘  └─────────────────┘\\r\\n48 | ```\\r\\n49 | \\r\\n50 | ### Key Architectural Patterns\\r\\n51 | \\r\\n52 | **Lazy-Loading History**: `SessionManager.getMessages()` automatically loads from DB if memory queue is empty. This enables seamless session restoration without explicit load calls.\\r\\n53 | \\r\\n54 | **Command Pattern**: CLI commands are modular handlers in `src/cli/commands/`. To add a new command:\\r\\n55 | 1. Create handler in `commands/` implementing `CommandHandler` interface\\r\\n56 | 2. Register in `commands/index.ts` registry\\r\\n57 | 3. No changes needed to main CLI class\\r\\n58 | \\r\\n59 | **Mutable Context**: Commands receive `CommandContext` with wrapped values (`{ value: string }`) to allow mutations (sessionId changes, exit flag).\\r\\n60 | \\r\\n61 | ### Session Management\\r\\n62 | \\r\\n63 | - **Session ID**: User-specified or auto-generated (`session_${timestamp}`)\\r\\n64 | - **Multi-user**: Each session has a `userId`\\r\\n65 | - **Memory Queue**: In-memory `MessageQueue` per session for fast access\\r\\n66 | - **Persistence**: Messages persisted to MongoDB via `MessageRepository`\\r\\n67 | \\r\\n68 | ### Code Organization Rules\\r\\n69 | \\r\\n70 | **File Size Limit**: No source file should exceed **480 lines**. When a file approaches this limit, split it into smaller, focused modules.\\r\\n71 | \\r\\n72 | **Principles**:\\r\\n73 | - Each file should have a single, clear responsibility\\r\\n74 | - Extract related functionality into separate modules\\r\\n75 | - Use barrel files (`index.ts`) for clean imports\\r\\n76 | - Keep CLI commands and utilities focused and split when needed\\r\\n77 | \\r\\n78 | ### CLI Implementation Details\\r\\n79 | \\r\\n80 | The CLI uses **Node.js native `readline`** with built-in history support:\\r\\n81 | - Up/Down arrows navigate input history\\r\\n82 | - History persisted in `InputHistory` class (max 100 entries)\\r\\n83 | - Spinner (`ora`) is used during LLM calls - safely terminates before readline resumes\\r\\n84 | \\r\\n85 | ### Provider Interface\\r\\n86 | \\r\\n87 | To add a new LLM provider, extend `LLMProvider` abstract class from `src/providers/base.ts`:\\r\\n88 | - Implement `generate(messages, options)` method\\r\\n89 | - Pass to Agent constructor via `AgentConfig`\\r\\n90 | \\r\\n91 | ### Database Models\\r\\n92 | \\r\\n93 | - **Message**: `{ sessionId, userId, content, role, type, createdAt }`\\r\\n94 | - **Session**: `{ sessionId, userId, createdAt, updatedAt }`\\r\\n95 | \\r\\n96 | Compound index on `{ sessionId: 1, createdAt: 1 }` optimizes history queries.\\r\\n97 | \\r\\n98 | \\r\\n99 | ### Code File Index\\r\\n100 | Quickly locate key functions and files\\r\\n101 | ./ai-agent-v2/projectMap.md\",\n  \"range\": {\n    \"startLine\": 1,\n    \"endLine\": 101\n  }\n}",
